Input: {"question": "Who is the artist of the album \"Without You I'm Nothing\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0176-c48332460690:d00", "start": 0, "end": 132, "text": "Without You I'm Nothing (Placebo album) Without You I'm Nothing is the second studio album by English alternative rock band Placebo."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0176-c48332460690:d00", "start": 133, "end": 238, "text": "Recorded in mid-to-late 1998, it was released on 12 October 1998 by record labels Hut and Virgin Records."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0176-c48332460690:d00", "start": 239, "end": 399, "text": "The album was a critical and commercial success, peaking at number seven in the UK Albums Chart and at number 20 on the US \"Billboard\" Heatseekers Albums chart."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0176-c48332460690:d00", "start": 400, "end": 514, "text": "\"Without You I'm Nothing\" went platinum in the UK and gold in France and has sold over one million copies to date."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0176-c48332460690:d00", "start": 515, "end": 586, "text": "The album spawned five singles, including \"Pure Morning\" and \"You Don't"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0176-c48332460690:d01", "start": 0, "end": 279, "text": "thirteen-month tour accompanied the album ; during this tour Stefan Olsdal fell off the stage and broke his arm , whilst on the same evening Brian Molko slept in the same position for ten hours , waking up with a compressed vertebrae in his neck and with no feeling in his head ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0176-c48332460690:d01", "start": 280, "end": 408, "text": "[ 33 ] Track listing [ edit ] All lyrics are written by Brian Molko ; all music is composed by Placebo , except where noted No ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0176-c48332460690:d01", "start": 409, "end": 437, "text